config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Which updates of Renovate merge on their own
    accDescr: Every update, a major one too, waits a week after its release and then merges on its own once every check passes. An update that fixes a vulnerability comes at once and merges on its own. The weekly refresh of the lock files of npm and pip-compile keeps to versions a week old and merges on its own as well. The refresh of a package manager that can't keep to that age, such as Composer, brings the newest version of every indirect dependency, without a week of waiting, so it waits for the maintainer.

    update(["Update,<br>a major one too"])
    fix(["Fix of a vulnerability"])
    refresh(["Weekly refresh of the lock files<br>of npm and pip-compile"])
    composer(["Weekly refresh of the lock files<br>of Composer and the others"])
    week["A week after<br>its release"]
    checks{"Every check<br>passes"}
    merge["Merges on its own"]
    maintainer["Waits for<br>the maintainer"]

    update --> week --> checks
    fix -- "at once" --> checks
    refresh -- "versions a week old" --> checks
    checks --> merge
    composer -- "newest versions,<br>no week of waiting" --> maintainer

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class update,fix,refresh,composer,week,checks bot
    class maintainer person
    class merge done
